WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.066
A few numbers capture the paper.

00:00:02.146 --> 00:00:06.828
Solving k-hop needs depth equal to floor of log
base two of k plus two,

00:00:06.908 --> 00:00:11.456
and that formula holds both in the proof and in the
trained networks.

00:00:11.536 --> 00:00:15.011
Adding a single layer roughly doubles the reach in k,

00:00:15.091 --> 00:00:18.365
so six layers cover everything up to sixteen hops.

00:00:18.445 --> 00:00:25.810
The simulation constants are clean too: an R-round
parallel protocol becomes a transformer of depth R plus one,

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:30.303
and any depth-L transformer collapses into order-L
parallel rounds.

00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:35.602
The contrast with other architectures is stark:
multi-layer recurrent networks,

00:00:35.682 --> 00:00:40.297
and by extension state-space models like Mamba,
need depth at least k,

00:00:40.377 --> 00:00:44.858
and so do efficient sub-quadratic attention
variants like Performer.

00:00:44.938 --> 00:00:49.620
Where the transformer is logarithmic in k, the
alternatives are linear.
